# AI Voicebot Implementation Roadmap

This plan is designed to help you transition from research-level model training to professional software engineering. We will build this project carefully, step-by-step, ensuring you understand *why* we are structuring it this way.

## Learning Objectives
1. **System & Architecture:** Understand how to decouple ML logic from web server logic.
2. **Model Serving:** Learn how to wrap heavy models (like Whisper and BERT) into classes so they are loaded into memory exactly once.
3. **API Engineering:** Master building RESTful endpoints using FastAPI so your AI can be queried over the web by any frontend.

---

## Step-by-Step Build Plan

### Phase 1: The Foundation (Environment & Core Utilities)
Before writing any AI code, professional engineers set up robust foundations.
* **Goal:** Create a reproducible environment, set up logging to track system states, and create a configuration manager.
* **Tasks:**
  * [ ] Create `requirements.txt` to lock our dependencies.
  * [ ] Build `core/logger.py` to handle all our system console and file logging.
  * [ ] Build `core/config.py` using `pydantic-settings` to securely handle application configurations and `.env` variables.

### Phase 2: The ML Engine (Model Wrapping)
We will take your underlying models and wrap them in clean Python classes. This makes debugging easier and allows the API to safely interact with them.
* **Goal:** Create Object-Oriented wrappers around the ASR, Intent Classification, and TTS systems.
* **Tasks:**
  * [ ] Develop `ml_models/asr_whisper.py` — A class that loads the Whisper model and implements a `.transcribe(audio_file)` method.
  * [ ] Develop `ml_models/intent_bert.py` — A class that loads your fine-tuned BERT and uses a `.predict(text)` method.
  * [ ] Develop `ml_models/tts_engine.py` — A class that implements a `.generate_audio(text)` method (using gTTS or Coqui).

### Phase 3: The Web API (FastAPI Integration)
We will bind the ML classes we built in Phase 2 to a high-performance web server.
* **Goal:** Expose your local models so that they can receive audio/text requests via standard HTTP POST calls.
* **Tasks:**
  * [ ] Build `api/main.py` — The core setup file for the FastAPI application, handling app startup events (which is when we will load the models into RAM).
  * [ ] Build `api/routes.py` — The HTTP endpoints (e.g., `/transcribe`, `/predict-intent`) that take a user's request, pass data to the ML models, and return JSON.

### Phase 4: End-to-End Testing
* **Goal:** Verify that the system works efficiently as a cohesive unit.
* **Tasks:**
  * [ ] Test individual endpoints via FastAPI's built-in Swagger UI (`http://localhost:8000/docs`).
  * [ ] Run an end-to-end chain: Audio -> Whisper -> Text -> BERT -> Intent & Response -> TTS Audio.

### Phase 5: The Interface (Vanilla Web Frontend)
* **Goal:** Build a beautiful, real-world frontend interface so any user can actually talk to the Voicebot without developer tools! We will use raw HTML, CSS, and JS (No React required!).
* **Tasks:**
  * [ ] Create `frontend/index.html` — The structural shell of the web app with a central glowing microphone button.
  * [ ] Create `frontend/style.css` — High-end, premium styling using a dark-mode glassmorphism design language.
  * [ ] Create `frontend/app.js` — The logic to physically capture microphone audio from the user's browser, send it to your `POST /chat` endpoint, and play the returned `.mp3` audio response automatically!
  * [ ] Update `api/main.py` with CORS middleware so your frontend is allowed to talk to your backend safely.

![Voicebot Frontend Mockup](C:\Users\hp5cd\.gemini\antigravity\brain\ac656c0c-cdfc-45c4-9b5f-9f2fe8ec1694\voicebot_ui_mockup_1775981696028.png)

### Phase 6: Level Up to Agentic AI
* **Goal:** To make this an advanced resuming-building project, we will replace the rigid intent classifier with a true reasoning Agent (LLM) that can hold conversations and use tools!
* **Tasks:**
  * [ ] Replace the BERT Intent model with an LLM framework (like Langchain or direct Groq/OpenAI calls).
  * [ ] Give the Voicebot "Tools" so it can look things up on the internet or check a database.

